<Layout title="Spanish Immigration Regulation changes 2026 | López Márquez Abogados" description="Overview of Royal Decree 316/2026 and its relevance to regularisation, residence and family matters in Spain.">
<PageHero eyebrow="Legal updates · Immigration" title="Important changes to Spain’s Immigration Regulation in 2026" description="Royal Decree 316/2026 changed several immigration rules, so the current wording and the applicant’s dates matter." primaryLabel="Review my situation" primaryHref="/en/contact" secondaryLabel="Immigration services" secondaryHref="/en/immigration" note="Published: 15 April 2026 · Effective: 16 April 2026 · Primary source: BOE." />
<section class="section"><div class="container prose"><h2>What changed</h2><p>Royal Decree 316/2026 amended several provisions of Spain’s Immigration Regulation, including rules on residence authorisations and exceptional circumstances, and added provisions concerning family members of Spanish citizens. It took effect on 16 April 2026.</p><h2>Applications already filed</h2><p>The decree contains transitional rules for certain applications filed before it took effect or already being processed. Do not apply the new requirements automatically without checking the route and filing date.</p><h2>What needs checking</h2><ul><li>The dates and continuity of the applicant’s stay in Spain.</li><li>The type of residence authorisation or regularisation route that may apply.</li><li>Relevant family relationships.</li><li>The filing date and current status of an application.</li><li>Available documents.</li></ul><p><a href="https://www.boe.es/eli/es/rd/2026/04/14/316" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read Royal Decree 316/2026 at the BOE →</a></p></div></section><CTA title="Has the applicable rule changed for your case?" text="Tell us what changed and we will start from the current regulation and relevant dates." label="Contact the firm" /></Layout>
